:\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-219/attest/specs/219/spec.md\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1037,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32641,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1037},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0dd7ed4f-100c-4188-9a34-077aa0b6aa25\",\"uuid\":\"401babe4-ee86-419a-8bd6-54a1c98ce637\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T02:07:50.440Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CfREanemkASkEfbkMMM9y\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_018kkd26j3fD4vvzyr15Yohz\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-219/attest/specs/219/spec.md\"}}}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_018kkd26j3fD4vvzyr15Yohz\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t## Problem\\n2\\t\\n3\\tAfter R2 a pass starts a stage and a worker runs it, but nothing in the product starts a stage again. A build whose worker died is recovered as `died` and then waits for a person; a review the vendor refused at capacity is a `failed` record, a counsel run, a filed issue, and two presses (#194's `verify-01`); a build whose head a required check rejected is a level (`blocked-on-checks`) that never becomes a record, so the item sits until someone reads the screen (#206's `build-01`, red on `typecheck`); a review that returns blocking findings stops the item as if the findings were a question for the operator. Every one of these is a failure whose answer does not touch the definition of done, and the project's rule is that such a failure needs the operator only if the spec must change. Nothing bounds a stage's wall clock either: a review on an adapter that streams no events is judged by a stall bound it can never trip, and the only ceiling is the operator's patience.\\n4\\t\\n5\\tThis is R3 of the reconciler (`claude/reconciler-brief-2026-09-20.md`, ruling C with its two amendments, section 6; the nine rulings of 2026-09-25 recorded in `claude/r3-rulings-2026-09-25.md`). It adds the retry families, one budget, the early stop, the exhaustion report, the stage ceilings, and the input the next attempt is handed; it retires the operator as the only thing that ever runs a stage twice.\\n6\\t\\n7\\tThe families. A stage record that is not a pass belongs to one of four retryable families or to a person. `died` and `hung` (recovery's classes, unchanged) and `transient` (new: a vendor's capacity, rate, or 5xx refusal, classed by the adapter on its report line as every class is) retry plainly: the next pass starts the next attempt, asks counsel nothing, and a `transient` waits `[drive].retry_after_s` (default 300) from i","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/davidbean/.claude/projects/-Users-davidbean-Projects-attavo-worktree-219/ae622d81-efb9-4dda-92a0-5ebf75b0d73f/tool-results/be1sjyers.txt","persistedOutputSize":733791}}
