{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 127\ncommit 7fb8a9b913f3f9937ce198715a533f5d7f8ad13e\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Fri Sep 25 22:58:59 2026 -0600\n\n    attavo: build #219, the reconciler's R3 -- retries, budgets, ceilings\n    \n    Four retryable families -- died, hung, transient (new: a vendor's\n    capacity, rate, or 5xx refusal, classed on the adapter's own report\n    line), and returned (new: a required check a passed build's head\n    rejected, or a review's own blocking finding) -- retry with no\n    operator, no counsel, inside one shared [drive].attempts budget per\n    stage; a transient waits [drive].retry_after_s first. Every other\n    non-pass record still reaches counsel as before, and an \"answer\"\n    verdict now starts the next attempt steered by it (retry_of and steer\n    on the record); \"patch\" and \"person\" stay the operator's, and a\n    question, a claims-boundary stop, a gate refusal, and an environment\n    refusal are never retried by this item regardless of what counsel\n    rules.\n    \n    Two attempts of one stage ending with the identical stop.signature\n    (a class's own detail or last event, digits stripped) stop the stage\n    early. A stopped, exhausted stage's report carries every attempt's\n    class, signature, bound, wall clock, and cost side by side, whether\n    the last two signatures match, and the rulings available -- --again\n    (retired inside the budget to a no-op that says the pass retries on\n    its own; forces the next attempt, marked again_by, once the budget or\n    the early stop has closed it) and amending the spec.\n    \n    [drive.build].ceiling_s and [drive.verify].ceiling_s bound a stage's\n    wall clock from its own marker; alive past it is hung by the ceiling\n    whatever event age says, and an adapter whose conformance.json\n    declares \"streams_events\": false is judged by the ceiling alone. The\n    doctor refuses a manifest that sets [drive] without both ceilings and\n    attempts, as it already refuses one without stall_after_s.\n    \n    A concluded red required check on a passed build's head is now a\n    returned review record the report writes on its own, not the\n    blocked-on-checks level with nothing behind it (#206's own build-01);\n    the next build is handed the check's log through\n    [forge].check_log_command. tests/test_drive.py's two tests that\n    encoded that level are rewritten to the record; #194's own verify-01,\n    a counsel run on a vendor's capacity error, is retired by the\n    transient family it would be classed as today.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n adapters/claude-code/conformance.json |   8 +\n adapters/claude-code/run              |  25 ++\n adapters/codex/conformance.json       |  11 +\n adapters/codex/run                    |  24 ++\n---\n(eval):1: operation not permitted: ps","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NTSv7eNjZaR164CKCNdfbr"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"061dd881-711c-41db-8604-438f84ab7c7d","uuid":"86b97bde-9958-46ba-a1af-21fbb16e7254","timestamp":"2026-09-26T05:07:50.596Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 127\ncommit 7fb8a9b913f3f9937ce198715a533f5d7f8ad13e\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Fri Sep 25 22:58:59 2026 -0600\n\n    attavo: build #219, the reconciler's R3 -- retries, budgets, ceilings\n    \n    Four retryable families -- died, hung, transient (new: a vendor's\n    capacity, rate, or 5xx refusal, classed on the adapter's own report\n    line), and returned (new: a required check a passed build's head\n    rejected, or a review's own blocking finding) -- retry with no\n    operator, no counsel, inside one shared [drive].attempts budget per\n    stage; a transient waits [drive].retry_after_s first. Every other\n    non-pass record still reaches counsel as before, and an \"answer\"\n    verdict now starts the next attempt steered by it (retry_of and steer\n    on the record); \"patch\" and \"person\" stay the operator's, and a\n    question, a claims-boundary stop, a gate refusal, and an environment\n    refusal are never retried by this item regardless of what counsel\n    rules.\n    \n    Two attempts of one stage ending with the identical stop.signature\n    (a class's own detail or last event, digits stripped) stop the stage\n    early. A stopped, exhausted stage's report carries every attempt's\n    class, signature, bound, wall clock, and cost side by side, whether\n    the last two signatures match, and the rulings available -- --again\n    (retired inside the budget to a no-op that says the pass retries on\n    its own; forces the next attempt, marked again_by, once the budget or\n    the early stop has closed it) and amending the spec.\n    \n    [drive.build].ceiling_s and [drive.verify].ceiling_s bound a stage's\n    wall clock from its own marker; alive past it is hung by the ceiling\n    whatever event age says, and an adapter whose conformance.json\n    declares \"streams_events\": false is judged by the ceiling alone. The\n    doctor refuses a manifest that sets [drive] without both ceilings and\n    attempts, as it already refuses one without stall_after_s.\n    \n    A concluded red required check on a passed build's head is now a\n    returned review record the report writes on its own, not the\n    blocked-on-checks level with nothing behind it (#206's own build-01);\n    the next build is handed the check's log through\n    [forge].check_log_command. tests/test_drive.py's two tests that\n    encoded that level are rewritten to the record; #194's own verify-01,\n    a counsel run on a vendor's capacity error, is retired by the\n    transient family it would be classed as today.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n adapters/claude-code/conformance.json |   8 +\n adapters/claude-code/run              |  25 ++\n adapters/codex/conformance.json       |  11 +\n adapters/codex/run                    |  24 ++\n---\n(eval):1: operation not permitted: ps"}
